  "_doc": "Moral choices offered by interactables. 'context' groups deeds by where they appear. blocked_by_flag hides the deed once a world flag is set. 'days' is how long the deed takes. effects use the shared effect keys; optional 'requires' {min_realm (realm id), min_alignment, max_alignment, flag (world flag), sect (SECT-006: a sects.json id, or \"any\" for any sect member)} shows the deed disabled with a reason until met; optional 'cooldown_days' (int >= 1) blocks repeating the deed until that many days have passed, optional 'favor' {npc_id: int} (C-380) changes that named villager's favor when the deed is done (GameState.perform_deed), optional 'result' (string, <= 140 chars) is posted after it, optional 'hint' (GUIDE-256; string 1..40 chars, only on deeds with 'favor': imperative phrase like \"bail out his leaking skiff\" that the guidance hint uses verbatim for the errand), optional 'once' (bool) allows it only once per life; optional 'enemy' (enemies.json id) must be beaten before the effects apply (losing ends the attempt, effects not applied); \"witnessed\": true means people saw it, so sects' reputation reacts to the alignment change (data/sects.json deed_scale).",
